Jean Frederic Frenet was a Fench mathematican, astronomer, and meteoologist. 
He is best known for being an independant co-discover of the Frenet-Serret formulas. 
He wrote six outof the nine formulas, which at that time where not expressed in vector notation. 
These formulas are important in the theory of space curves (differential geometry), and they were presented in his doctoral thesis at Toulouse in 1847. 
